\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The two sonars of the vehicle in a karst conduit. The horizontal sonar (blue) turns about the vertical axis and sweeps a horizontal plane all around the vehicle; its beam is narrow horizontally but $25^\circ $ high, so it covers a wide band of the wall at once (vertical blue arrow). The vertical sonar (green) turns about the longitudinal axis of the vehicle and sweeps a cross-section of the conduit with a narrow beam. The curved arrows show the rotation of each sonar head.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bg_scanplanes}{{3}{5}{The two sonars of the vehicle in a karst conduit. The horizontal sonar (blue) turns about the vertical axis and sweeps a horizontal plane all around the vehicle; its beam is narrow horizontally but $25^\circ $ high, so it covers a wide band of the wall at once (vertical blue arrow). The vertical sonar (green) turns about the longitudinal axis of the vehicle and sweeps a cross-section of the conduit with a narrow beam. The curved arrows show the rotation of each sonar head}{figure.3}{}}
